      "math_academy_id": "e-15058",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(6)$ given below, compute $P(X=7).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ | $\\,0.7440\\,$ | $\\,0.8472\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\})+P(X=7) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =F(6)+P(X=7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =F(7)-F(6) \\\\  & =0.7440-0.6063 \\\\  & =0.1377.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14164071/observations/step-e15058-1ea14a7cd8eae0b587a4.html",
